                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 D 74/238: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commissioner at Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Young</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-04T12:00:00+01:36"><hi rendition="#italic">August 4,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 5:17 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>91. Mrs. Doty formerly prisoner in Petrograd reported at consulate August 2nd and
                    left town immediately. She left Russia about July 1st in company with other
                    Americans.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Young</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
